      "writtenOn": "2022-12-20T16:36:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So a path that is convex we are considering simple? What if a client only sets kPath draw type? I feel like Skia\u0027s api is setup in a way where we say things like drawOval, drawRRect, etc. are just short hand notations for drawPaths with those specific verbs (i.e. path.addRect(...)). Seems like if they say drawPath they should be able to draw any shape. Like if a client does\n```\nSkPath path;\npath.addCircle();\nSkCanvas::drawPath(path);\n```\nI believe we will sniff out the path is just a simple circle and go down our \"simple\" code paths for a circle.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 45,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 45,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "cb2970ae5b3d8316521831ca55d027683ad0572a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a1a53f95_1169c562",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/RendererProvider.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
